<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Apple Pay entitlement — staged and deliberately NOT wired into the build.

  The app's Apple Pay is the *embedded* MyFatoorah flow (MFApplePayButton →
  MFSDK.loadApplePay): the button is MyFatoorah's own Apple Pay page inside a
  WKWebView, running under THEIR merchant identity and certificates. Their
  support confirmed (2026-08-26) that embedded needs no merchant id, no
  payment-processing certificate, and no activation on our side — so this
  entitlement must stay out of CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS, where it would only
  break automatic signing against a merchant id that does not exist.

  The embedded sheet requires iOS 16+ (Apple Pay in WKWebView); on older
  devices the panel hides the button after two failed arms and the card form
  carries on. Turning the button on is server-side only: store option
  `zooboxi_apple_pay_native` = yes — no app release involved.

  Keep this file ONLY for a possible future native PassKit path (MFApplePay /
  applePayPayment). That path — and only that path — needs the full chain:
  Apple merchant id `merchant.com.zooboxi.store`, a payment-processing
  certificate minted from MyFatoorah's CSR, and this file wired into the
  three Runner build configurations.
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.in-app-payments</key>
	<array>
		<string>merchant.com.zooboxi.store</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
